    "8c688c0d63daa54fd29e49fbb5ce07c9e7d66da943013395f9c038df942460b2": {
      "text": "{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The user wants me to execute a sequence of 10 steps designed to exercise all available tool categories. I must stay within the current directory and use dedicated tools when they are preferred or available, falling back to shell commands otherwise.\\n\\nStep 1: List files. Use `read` or `bash ls`. `bash ls` is fine.\\nStep 2: Create `notes.md`. Use a dedicated write tool (`write`).\\nStep 3: Read `notes.md`. Use `read`.\\nStep 4: Edit `notes.md`. Use a dedicated edit tool (`edit`).\\nStep 5: Find files starting with \\\"note\\\". Use `bash find`.\\nStep 6: Search contents for \\\"fixture\\\". Use `bash grep -r`.\\nStep 7: Read a non-existent file. Use `read`. Expect failure report.\\nStep 8: Create and run a script `count.sh`. Use `write` and `bash`.\\nStep 9: Sub-agent dispatch. Check for dedicated sub-agent tool. If none, skip and report.\\nStep 10: Summarize. Final response.\\n\\nLet's start with Step 1.\",\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"text\":\"**Step 1: List the files in the current directory**\\n\\nI will use the `bash` tool with the `ls` command to list the files in the current directory, as this is a standard and reliable way to fulfill this request.\\n\\n\",\"type\":\"text\"},{\"args\":{\"command\":\"ls\"},\"toolCallId\":\"call_9g4skz92\",\"toolName\":\"bash\",\"type\":\"tool-call\"}],\"id\":\"32022bf5\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}"
    },
    "8dbe12403af0df15bd37f14336de2b24007ee9a30f5fbb22003c71d178145278": {
      "text": "{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"**Step 8: Write and run `count.sh`**\\n\\nI used the `write` tool to create `count.sh` with a shell loop, and then executed it using `bash count.sh`. The output confirmed that the script prints the numbers 1 through 5 on separate lines, resulting in exactly five lines of output.\\n\\nStep 9: Sub-agent dispatch.\\nI checked my available tools and found no dedicated sub-agent or task-dispatch tool. Therefore, I must skip this step and report it explicitly.\\n\\nStep 10: Summarize.\\nI will now summarize the entire process.\\n<channel|>**Step 9: Sub-agent dispatch**\\n\\nI do not have a dedicated sub-agent or task-dispatch tool available, so I must skip this step.\\n\\n**Step 10: Summary**\\n\\nI successfully completed a sequence of tasks designed to exercise various tool functionalities. I started by listing directory contents, creating and reading a markdown file (`notes.md`). I then practiced content modification using the `edit` tool, followed by searching the filesystem (`find`) and file contents (`grep`). I demonstrated graceful error handling by attempting to read a non-existent file. Finally, I created and ran a shell script to confirm sequential output, fulfilling all the outlined steps.\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"id\":\"ce78e79b\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}"
    },
